WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.100
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.650
Nou, City of Itoigawa, Niigata Prefecture

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:10.770
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.590
Turn out well.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:13.280
Please turn out well.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.800
probably helped me notice that

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.470
At last, it’s the final match, huh?

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.430
probably helped me notice that

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.510
Yeah.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:19.320
The locale is Nou, in the city Of Itoigawa, Niigata prefecture.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.980
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.770
The theme is Japan’s bread.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.440
Truly appropriate for the final match.
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.270
Truly appropriate for the final match.

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:27.270
Right now, Pantasia has three panels.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.650
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.650
If we capture the final panel,

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.330
the St. Pierre panel in the center will be
sandwiched in between and we can recapture it.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.530
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.160
It’ll give us a big comeback victory.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.120
Yeah, but only if we win.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:40.210
But should we lose, we will lose miserably with a score of 6-3.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.200
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.120
No way!

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.460
Azuma-san is bound to win!

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:46.600
After all, this is Azuma-san’s place of birth, Niigata.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.920
that white sky with my colors.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.630
Do you honestly think so, Tsukino?

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:52.130
that white sky with my colors.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.100
After all, our opponent is Kirisaki Yuuichi’s son...

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.260
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.440
Meister Kirisaki!

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.060
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.220
Azuma-kun...

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.780
I will not lose this match.
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:04.000
I will not lose this match.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.500
Who is it that you will give truly delicious bread to!?

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.580
The <i>Japan</i>, forever!

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:21.460
Azuma!

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:22.960
If you lose, I’m giving you a whooping.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.000
You got that?

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.090
Nii-san...

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:31.440
Why are you helping that man?

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:33.940
That demon...

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:39.560
He devoured bread right in front
of us, even as we were starving.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.070
Say, Sophie-san...

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:45.190
I’ve been wondering about this
ever since we were in Monaco, but...

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:50.450
After experiencing something that
traumatic, why did you become a baker?

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.470
Th-That’s...

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.540
And not just you...

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.970
In the end, even your brother became a baker.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:02.230
That’s because the bread from
that time really looked delicious!

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:06.260
It made me think that I wanted
to make a bread like that someday.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:11.800
So, in the end, the two of you
have followed in your father’s footsteps.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:16.890
So isn’t it just that, somewhere deep in
your hearts, you just love your father?

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:18.940
Of course not!

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.350
All we desired was the bread.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:25.070
We’ve never acknowledged that... demon!

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.610
I can already see what the
outcome of this battle will be.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.410
Even at the stage of ingredient selection,

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:38.410
St. Pierre’s Meister Kirisaki has
only chosen the highest quality.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.880
The pure water, melted from the snow of the Alps...

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.420
Rice flour made of Omanta rice,

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.550
a product made with further selection of koshi-hikari grains

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:51.050
and raised in the fertile soil of
Nou, Itoigawa city, Niigata prefecture.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:55.560
And he’s liberally using crab miso and meat from the ultimate Nou specialty product,

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:59.270
Red Snow crab, harvested from the
stormy waters of the Sea of Japan.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.650
In comparison, the ingredients Azuma is using are...

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:05.690
some nameless variety of rice
raised by Azuma’s grandfather and...

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.780
mugwort and miso from Nou.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:11.240
You can’t help but think that he gave up
on winning the match against Meister

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:14.790
and decided to make his
family happy by using their stuff.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.530
Hey guys...

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:18.800
You’re sure that Kazuma will win, right?

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.210
Of course!

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:24.920
Kazuma is using the consummate
organic rice that I grew, the <i>Japan</i> rice.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.050
And in his dough, he’s mixing the wild mugwort

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:29.420
that I went and picked from the hills behind our home.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:36.800
And he’s using the petalite stone for <i>Japan</i>
#44 that I have now perfected and remade.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.070
There’s no way he can lose now!

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.310
Well, I certainly hope so.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.100
To send out Meister Kirisaki...

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:48.650
Looks like he’s getting into dotage.

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:51.870
And on top of that, he won’t let
me sabotage the match at all...

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:55.740
At this rate, there’s no room for action for me.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:57.870
And it’s the last episode!

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.200
Why?!

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:00.750
Kawachi-san!

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.890
Why is Meister participating on St. Pierre’s side?

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.880
That is definitely a mystery.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:10.550
Because I believe that Meister
hates his father, Kirisaki Yuuichi.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.400
You don’t understand?!

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:13.640
Suwabara!

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.590
Even if it means that you have to camp with the enemy,

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:20.150
if there’s a strong opponent you want
to defeat, you will want to battle him.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.680
Just like Kai from the past.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:24.980
In other words, Azuma has...

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:29.870
matured to the point that he can move the
heart of a man of Meister Kirisaki’s talent.

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:33.700
Well, it’s true that he’s grown to a fearsome level.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:38.410
Yeah, before I knew it, he’d
completely outdistanced me.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.370
Though a certain person had been
outstripped from the very beginning.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:42.870
And who might you be referring to?

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.080
It couldn’t be me, right?

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:47.600
Come to think of it, when did it stop?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.210
What’s that?

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:53.100
Some time ago, Azuma-san stopped
saying “<i>Japan</i> number something”...

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:55.050
Now that you mention it...

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:58.090
I believe that he was still
saying it during the Monaco Cup.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:04:59.610
Oh I see!

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:03.520
During Yakitate!! 9,
he hasn’t said it even once!

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:04.730
Tsukino!

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:06.060
I take back my words!

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:06.410
Huh?

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:10.690
It just might be that Azuma will
defeat the Kirisaki father and son.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:11.650
Really?!

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:13.620
Why do you say that?!

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:17.280
Until then, his <i>Japan</i>s had been trial products.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.110
But...

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:22.600
Lately, he’s not been calling his
creations <i>Japan</i> number somethings!

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:26.540
In other words, it means that he’s completed his <i>Japan</i>!

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:31.960
It’s done.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:33.680
It’s complete.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:42.610
Both smell really good.

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:45.850
Old Man... I mean Mister Kuroyanagi...

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:47.730
Could you eat mine first?

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:51.360
Bread baked with petalite
is most delicious when fresh.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:53.120
Petalite?

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:54.690
I see...

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.540
It’s the bread that sends you to heaven...

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.290
I don’t mind being second.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:00.320
No.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:03.990
I will sample Meister Kirisaki’s Omanta <i>Gopan</i> first.

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:09.210
Because, if I go to heaven, I won’t be
able to judge the second bread right away.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:11.350
N-No way!

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:11.920
Please judge mine, will you?!

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:13.290
This is bad...

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.850
Not judging it while it is still fresh...

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:18.970
No, that’s not the only worry we have.

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:24.760
You never know what crazy reaction
Kuro-yan will have with the Omanta <i>Gopan</i>.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:28.350
But it’s the final episode after all,
so it doesn’t really matter, right?

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.190
You moron!

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:32.830
If things go wrong, the broadcast
might have to be canceled midway through!

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:37.570
Well then, starting with
Meister Kirisaki’s Omanta <i>Gopan</i>.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.590
Omanta...

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:52.500
This song is Omanta-bayashi by Minami Haruo!

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.500
This is Kuro-yan’s reaction?

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.760
Looks like a pretty straightforward one...

00:06:57.760 --> 00:06:58.970
Quiet, Baldy!

00:06:58.970 --> 00:06:59.260
Huh?!

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:02.140
What the...

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:03.680
A... A stingray?!

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:05.780
Why has Kuro-yan become a stingray?!

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:08.020
You have holes where you should have eyes?

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:11.780
This isn’t just any old stingray...
It’s a giant ray, the manta ray!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.620
Manta?

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.070
Oh, manta!

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:15.790
Omanta!

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.480
Omanta <i>Gopan</i>!

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:20.190
Exactly.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:22.110
Hey, wait!

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:23.110
Where are you going?!

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:25.240
Azuma’s judging is still left!

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:27.330
You dimwitted baldy!

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:28.540
Mantas are seawater fish!

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:32.210
They have to swim the seven seas of the world freely!

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:34.120
Farewell!

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.210
He went off.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.970
But thankfully, the broadcast didn’t get canceled.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:43.050
I suppose we should count our blessings.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:44.590
But what are we going to do?

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:49.220
If the judge disappears,
what happens with the match?

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:51.810
Do we have a substitute for Kuro-yan?

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:53.490
You don’t have to worry about that.

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.190
In case of unforeseen problems,

00:07:55.190 --> 00:08:01.250
should Kuroyanagi be unable to judge,
I’m supposed to take over.

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:03.700
What are you talking about?!

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.910
You’re from the St. Pierre side!

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:11.080
At this time I am the owner
of both St. Pierre and Pantasia.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.210
Therefore, I will make a fair judgment.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:14.420
Please wait!

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:19.920
It’s true that the owner will judge as
the substitute according to the rule book.

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:22.720
But, I believe that it is a requirement

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:27.930
that an additional person unrelated to
both St. Pierre and Pantasia also be involved.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:32.640
I’ve memorized every nook and corner of the rule book.

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:34.410
You cannot fool us.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:35.900
That’s all right with me.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:40.030
But only if you can produce such a judge immediately.

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:41.910
And I think that it’s not a good idea for you guys

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:42.030
to let Azuma-kun’s bread cool any more than this.

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.150
Eat it quickly!
to let Azuma-kun’s bread cool any more than this.

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:47.410
to let Azuma-kun’s bread cool any more than this.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:51.120
Anyone will do!

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:53.290
Just eat my <i>Japan</i> quickly!

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:54.750
What should we do?

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:59.630
At this rate, we might have to
depend on Kirisaki alone to do the judging...

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:02.770
This is...

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.220
According to Monaco legend,

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:10.390
if you have that ring, a
legendary hero will appear before you.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:14.560
Right now, I have no choice
but to pray to the Pierron ring.

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:18.610
I beg of you, O Legendary Hero.

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:23.400
Please taste the bread that has all
our hopes in it... Azuma-san’s bread...

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:25.370
Wh-What’s that?!

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:26.490
It’s a bird!

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:27.280
It’s a plane!

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:29.840
No! That’s Pierrot!

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.470
Pii-errot-errot-errot!

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.910
The legendary hero was Pierrot-san?!

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:36.580
Pierrot!

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:39.080
Yep, now that you’ve called
upon me, you can rest at ease!

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.850
Come, let’s start the judging shall we?

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.840
Old Ma... I mean Mister Pierrot...

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:47.480
Mr. Kirisaki... Are you all right with this?

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.180
The crown prince of the Kingdom of Monaco, huh?

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:53.520
He has no shortcomings for the final match.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:54.440
Fine.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:55.490
All right!

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:58.440
Now, please eat my <i>Japan</i>.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.210
Pi...

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:13.470
errot.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:19.870
Th-This is...

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:29.340
Hey, you’re quite talented at this.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:31.030
Come on, give it some more work.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:31.890
Okay!

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:33.350
That’s good! Just like that.

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:36.030
Why are we in an image from 10 years ago?!

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:37.350
This is...

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.020
My past.

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:44.240
Then why is there a young Azuma here?

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:46.820
This child was Azuma Kazuma?

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:49.360
I was right...

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:53.070
When I returned from France...

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:56.920
To be honest, I didn’t have the confidence to
manage in Tokyo, so I ran to my hometown.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:01.580
I left something behind in order to come back, too...

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:04.790
But, it’s different now.

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:07.050
Watching you try so hard...

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:08.840
I cannot lose, either.

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:09.730
That’s what I thought.

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:13.070
Will I... ever see you again?

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:16.760
If you aspire to be a baker from now on,

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:21.310
and are able to continue
pursuing your dream of <i>Japan</i>...

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:24.580
we may be able to meet again one day.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:25.960
Why?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.290
Why were you kind back then?

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:32.920
After that, when you perfected
the <i>Gopan</i> instead of the <i>Japan</i>,

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:36.930
why didn’t you try to help
Azuma when he came to Tokyo?

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:39.300
Why did you try to crush him instead?

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:44.060
<i>Japan</i>, is it?

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:47.520
I guess just about anyone
can come up with the name, eh?

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:49.020
Ridiculous.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:52.400
The reason why I want to crush Japan is...

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.860
because I HATE <i>Japan</i>.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:58.070
I’m sorry, but...

00:11:58.070 --> 00:11:59.740
I can’t shake hands with you, old man.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:03.290
The curtain is raised
on the final showdown!

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:05.040
Why?

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:08.040
Why did you need to do this?

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:11.290
You wouldn’t understand
even if I told you.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:16.420
Wh-What happened?

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:17.510
I... don’t know.

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:21.390
If it’s all right...

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:26.230
I’d like to request that you try my <i>Gopan</i> this time.

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:33.900
Gladly!

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:41.490
Omanta...

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.030
This again?!

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:58.720
Sorry for the wait, Azuma.

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:02.340
I just completed swimming
freely in the seven seas of the world.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:03.680
Oh I see...

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:05.680
That was bloody fast!

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:09.810
But... in the meantime, Azuma’s
bread has completely cooled down.

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:17.280
<i>Japan</i>.

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:18.650
I see...

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.490
This was bloody fast too!

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:21.740
It’s already over?!

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:23.370
Looks like the match has been decided.

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:26.870
No, because of copyright issues,
both reactions are similar!

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:28.160
An impressive final match!

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:30.370
It’s a great battle!

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:34.880
Well then, with your permission,
I would like to announce the results.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.210
He’s speaking politely!

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:37.630
Kuro-yan’s speaking politely!

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:39.800
Shut your trap!

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:42.130
When did I ever speak politely?!

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:43.140
Just now!

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:44.850
You spoke politely just now!

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:46.350
What was that?!

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:49.640
It’s my policy to never judge
preferentially or speak politely!

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:52.310
Well then, let’s explain from the very beginning.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:53.520
Explain what?!

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:56.980
Starting with Meister Kirisaki’s <i>Gopan</i> from St. Pierre.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.150
It was truly delicious!

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:03.030
I stand in awe as to how the Omanta rice, wheat
and crab were added in a gradient fashion,

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:08.660
producing a bread with slight variations
that blended together in perfect harmony.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:11.870
And, the taste of baked crab was truly one of a kind!

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:16.500
People usually consider
boiling the best way to prepare crab!

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:20.880
But by directly baking fresh crab,
its original umami is concentrated.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:25.880
The aroma, together with the wonderful flavor
that spreads in your mouth, is truly transcendent.

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:28.140
That’s like a bloody rave review!

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.940
And, Azuma Kazuma’s <i>Japan</i>
from Pantasia was also delicious!

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:39.110
The bread dough that used the consummate
organic rice as the base was wonderful!

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:42.820
This is thanks to Grandpa Umatarou!

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:44.360
Right?

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:45.320
That’s great, Grandpa!

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:51.450
But! The flavor that surpassed even
that was the wild mugwort from Nou!

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.700
Unlike the cultivated stuff,

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:56.830
due to the presence of superior proteins, it
has a dense-flavor and a wonderful fragrance!

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:59.210
Thank you, Grandpa Umajirou!

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:01.590
Right? Right?

00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:03.220
Way to go, Grandpa Umajirou!

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:04.590
But! However!

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:07.760
This <i>Japan</i> has a special characteristic to its
baking that brought both these things to life.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.640
The petalite stone that emits a
high concentration of infrared rays

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.470
makes the bread delicious many times over!

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:16.060
I’m really grateful, Grandpa Umasaburou!

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:18.230
Right? Right? Right?

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:21.730
Bread baked with my petalite is #1 in Japan!

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.530
That’s awesome, Grandpa Umasaburou!

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:26.700
In addition to all that...
The most wonderful thing is...

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:30.280
the Nou miso mixed into the bread!

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:31.700
Brains, you say?!

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:32.950
No, Nou miso!

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:34.830
Nou miso!

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:38.290
A specialty product of this region,
made with Japan’s #1 Echigo rice,

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.620
the pure and clear water that flows in Fubikisando,

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.590
and the special soybean oil of emisuburi.

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.340
It is then placed into natural wood caskets,

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.180
and allowed to mature naturally.

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:49.420
No additives are used in it at all!

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:51.760
Yep! Thank you, Nou miso!

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.770
Hang in there guys!

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:56.850
And!

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:59.690
The thing that brought out the taste
of the Nou miso to its maximum is...

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:02.480
Azuma’s warm hands that kneaded the rice flour!

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:04.360
The Solar Hands!

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:09.450
The warmth spread the wild mugwort and the
fragrance of the miso thoroughly into the dough,

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:12.240
raising their harmony with the organic rice!

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.000
And! And!

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:19.710
The truly amazing thing about this bread is...

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:21.880
you take one bite and...

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:26.130
someone like me becomes serious and...

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:34.930
arrogant people like Kuroyanagi...
become courteous!

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:36.230
Please stop that.

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:38.220
I am such a person by nature.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:40.020
That is... In other words...

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:45.190
The Nou miso present in Azuma’s <i>Japan</i>
provides a stimulus to our brains...

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:48.740
having the effect of returning us
to our original personalities!

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:51.780
Is that why Kuro-yan was polite?

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.450
The fearsome <i>Japan</i>...

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:55.950
It goes without saying that the taste is magnificent.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:17:02.170
I believe that this greatly surpasses the bread
that once changed history, the Cannabis <i>Japan</i>!

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:03.960
Understood.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:05.670
Then, the result of your judgment is?

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:06.420
That’s right!

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:07.420
Which one is more delicious?

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:17.850
This match is...

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:20.690
A draw!

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:23.610
I can’t decide between the two breads either.

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:24.440
I’m sorry.

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:25.900
A draw?!

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:29.440
Then are we finished with the panels in the 5-3 state?

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:31.570
I wonder if they’ll have an additional match...?

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:32.950
No, we’ve lost.

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:37.080
According to the rule book,
once there is a substitute judge,

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:40.160
the three of them have to come up with a conclusion.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.250
If two of the judges claim a draw,

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:49.630
the third judge has the right to decide the match.

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:51.130
In other words...

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:56.180
Everything will be decided by
the third judge, Kirisaki Yuuichi.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.640
I suppose our loss is certain.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:17:59.850
Damn it!

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:02.350
I completely forgot about that old man’s existence!

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:06.110
You’ve completely forgotten about my existence too.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:11.320
We did it!

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:13.610
We’ve finally crushed those cockroaches!

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:15.490
W-We’ve lost.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:18.410
Pantasia will be taken over by Kirisaki!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.540
Sorry for the wait.

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:32.170
The results of my judging are...

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:35.550
The bread that I thought was delicious is...

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:40.810
Azuma Kazuma-kun’s Nou-miso <i>Japan</i> from Pantasia.

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:46.310
That’s Kirisaki’s true face?!

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:47.360
No way!

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:49.400
Such a kind face!

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:51.610
What the hell happened?!

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:53.030
Can something like this really happen?

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:58.120
That old man’s face...

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:00.700
I get the feeling I’ve seen it somewhere.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:01.200
Nou

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:06.080
Well then, I will now
announce the winner of Yakitate!! 9.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:10.800
With five panels vs. four, it is
the victory of the Pantasia team!

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:14.300
Yahoo!

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:16.300
We won!

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:18.100
We did it Tsukino!

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:21.140
Pantasia is now truly and officially all yours!

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:22.470
Yeah...

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:25.020
Thank you, Azuma-san.

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:27.980
He bloody won!

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:31.020
Against Meister Kirisaki,
whom even I couldn’t win against!

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:34.650
But, to think that he judged in our favor...

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:42.660
His hidden personality probably came forth
after he ate Azuma-kun’s Nou-miso <i>Japan</i>.

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:45.290
You mean to say that in reality, he’s...

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:46.670
Nii-san.

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:47.500
Sophie!

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.750
Silvan... Sophie...

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:54.880
Once, I asked you a certain question...

00:19:55.430 --> 00:19:58.090
If you’ve created a truly
delicious-looking bread,

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:01.680
who’s the first person you’d give it to?

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:02.770
Yes.

00:20:02.770 --> 00:20:04.480
The answer was “yourself.”

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:05.680
That’s right.

00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:09.940
Just because it looks delicious,
doesn’t mean it really is.

00:20:09.940 --> 00:20:12.980
In that case, you can’t give it to people yet.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:16.990
But, once you <i>know</i> that it’s delicious,
whom would you give it to first?

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:20.950
Who do you think it is?

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:22.620
Isn’t that obvious?

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:28.620
When you <i>know</i> that the bread is truly delicious...

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:33.880
I see. You want me to eat it, huh?

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:36.090
Me! It’s me, right Kazuma?

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:37.130
What are you talking about?

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.340
It obviously has to be me!

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:42.890
I hope you guys live long.

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:44.640
Huh? Me?

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:50.100
While I fought this battle primarily for myself,
it was also for your Pantasia, Tsukino.

00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:51.610
That’s correct.

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:55.650
You first give a truly delicious bread to...

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:58.450
every person you’d want to eat it.

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:02.780
And in addition, you want every
person who loves bread to eat it.

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:03.990
Yep!

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.790
Is that so?

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:07.330
Father...

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:09.000
Mr. Kirisaki...

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:13.250
I don’t believe that you consciously knew about
the Monaco Royal Family’s tradition, but...

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:17.840
Could it be that like the lion
who throws his cub into the valley,

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:22.510
you’ve been purposely playing the villain
for the sake of Japan’s bread industry?

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.600
Mr. Kirisaki...?

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:31.440
Of course not!

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:33.980
All I want is to make money.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:35.860
That’s all I make bread for.

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:40.150
What’s with the premature joy, folks?

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:43.910
I’ve only lost ownership of Pantasia.

00:21:43.910 --> 00:21:46.120
I still have St. Pierre.

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:48.950
It is now that the true battle begins!

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:50.580
He’s back to normal.

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:53.710
I guess the effect of the
Nou-miso <i>Japan</i> has worn off.

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:03.180
Azuma-san...

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:05.680
So, what happens now,
Azuma Kazuma-kun?

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:10.430
Is your <i>Japan</i> something that
will end at the stage it is now?

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:12.060
Are you kidding?

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:15.440
My <i>Japan</i> can still evolve yet further!

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:27.700
And I challenge you with my <i>Japan</i>!

00:22:44.170 --> 00:22:50.850
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:22:52.130 --> 00:22:58.770
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:22:59.890 --> 00:23:06.700
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:23:07.690 --> 00:23:14.610
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:23:14.610 --> 00:23:21.830
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:23:22.870 --> 00:23:31.320
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:40.220
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:23:40.220 --> 00:23:44.440
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:47.480
is the light of only you.

00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:50.970
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:56.240
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:23:56.240 --> 00:24:03.500
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?
